[
  {
    "device": "cabinet",
    "kind": "h2",
    "text": "29.6 Cabinet",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "29.6 Cabinet",
        "html_line": 662,
        "anchor": "cabinet",
        "section": "29.6"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 662,
    "anchor": "cabinet",
    "section": "29.6",
    "locator": "cabinet:B001"
  },
  {
    "device": "cabinet",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "Cabinet is an effect that emulates the sound of five classic guitar cabinets. Developed in collaboration with Softube, Cabinet uses physical modelling technology to provide a range of authentic sounds, with optimized mics and mic positioning.",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "29.6 Cabinet",
        "html_line": 662,
        "anchor": "cabinet",
        "section": "29.6"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 672,
    "anchor": null,
    "section": null,
    "locator": "cabinet:B002"
  },
  {
    "device": "cabinet",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "The Speaker chooser allows you to select from a variety of speaker sizes and combinations. The chooser’s entries indicate the number of speakers and the speaker size in inches. For example, ”4x12” means four 12-inch speakers. In the real world, more and larger speakers generally means higher volumes.",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "29.6 Cabinet",
        "html_line": 662,
        "anchor": "cabinet",
        "section": "29.6"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 672,
    "anchor": null,
    "section": null,
    "locator": "cabinet:B003"
  },
  {
    "device": "cabinet",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "The Microphone chooser changes the position of the virtual microphone in relation to the speaker cabinet. Near On-Axis micing results in a bright, focused sound, while Near Off-Axis is more resonant and a bit less bright. Choose the Far position for a balanced sound that also has some characteristics of the virtual ”room.”",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "29.6 Cabinet",
        "html_line": 662,
        "anchor": "cabinet",
        "section": "29.6"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 672,
    "anchor": null,
    "section": null,
    "locator": "cabinet:B004"
  },
  {
    "device": "cabinet",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "The switch below the Microphone chooser toggles between a Dynamic and Condenser mic. Dynamic mics are a bit grittier and commonly used when close-micing guitar cabinets because they are capable of handling much higher volumes. Condenser mics are more accurate, and are commonly used for micing from a distance. Of course, Cabinet’s virtual condenser mic won’t be damaged by high volume levels, so feel free to experiment.",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "29.6 Cabinet",
        "html_line": 662,
        "anchor": "cabinet",
        "section": "29.6"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 684,
    "anchor": null,
    "section": null,
    "locator": "cabinet:B005"
  },
  {
    "device": "cabinet",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "The Output switch toggles between mono and stereo (Dual) processing. Note that in Dual mode, Cabinet uses twice as much CPU.",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "29.6 Cabinet",
        "html_line": 662,
        "anchor": "cabinet",
        "section": "29.6"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 684,
    "anchor": null,
    "section": null,
    "locator": "cabinet:B006"
  },
  {
    "device": "cabinet",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "The Dry/Wet control adjusts the balance between the processed and dry signals.",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "29.6 Cabinet",
        "html_line": 662,
        "anchor": "cabinet",
        "section": "29.6"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 684,
    "anchor": null,
    "section": null,
    "locator": "cabinet:B007"
  },
  {
    "device": "cabinet",
    "kind": "h3",
    "text": "29.6.1 Cabinet Tips",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "29.6 Cabinet",
        "html_line": 662,
        "anchor": "cabinet",
        "section": "29.6"
      },
      {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "29.6.1 Cabinet Tips",
        "html_line": 684,
        "anchor": "cabinet-tips",
        "section": "29.6.1"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 684,
    "anchor": "cabinet-tips",
    "section": "29.6.1",
    "locator": "cabinet:B008"
  },
  {
    "device": "cabinet",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "Here are some tips for using Cabinet:",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "29.6 Cabinet",
        "html_line": 662,
        "anchor": "cabinet",
        "section": "29.6"
      },
      {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "29.6.1 Cabinet Tips",
        "html_line": 684,
        "anchor": "cabinet-tips",
        "section": "29.6.1"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 684,
    "anchor": null,
    "section": null,
    "locator": "cabinet:B009"
  },
  {
    "device": "cabinet",
    "kind": "h4",
    "text": "29.6.1.1 Amps and Cabinets",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "29.6 Cabinet",
        "html_line": 662,
        "anchor": "cabinet",
        "section": "29.6"
      },
      {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "29.6.1 Cabinet Tips",
        "html_line": 684,
        "anchor": "cabinet-tips",
        "section": "29.6.1"
      },
      {
        "level": 4,
        "text": "29.6.1.1 Amps and Cabinets",
        "html_line": 684,
        "anchor": "amps-and-cabinets-1",
        "section": "29.6.1.1"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 684,
    "anchor": "amps-and-cabinets-1",
    "section": "29.6.1.1",
    "locator": "cabinet:B010"
  },
  {
    "device": "cabinet",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "Guitar cabinets are normally fed by guitar amps. For this reason, Cabinet is paired with Amp, and the two are normally used together. But you can also achieve interesting and exotic sounds by using Amp and Cabinet separately.",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "29.6 Cabinet",
        "html_line": 662,
        "anchor": "cabinet",
        "section": "29.6"
      },
      {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "29.6.1 Cabinet Tips",
        "html_line": 684,
        "anchor": "cabinet-tips",
        "section": "29.6.1"
      },
      {
        "level": 4,
        "text": "29.6.1.1 Amps and Cabinets",
        "html_line": 684,
        "anchor": "amps-and-cabinets-1",
        "section": "29.6.1.1"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 684,
    "anchor": null,
    "section": null,
    "locator": "cabinet:B011"
  },
  {
    "device": "cabinet",
    "kind": "h4",
    "text": "29.6.1.2 Multiple mics",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "29.6 Cabinet",
        "html_line": 662,
        "anchor": "cabinet",
        "section": "29.6"
      },
      {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "29.6.1 Cabinet Tips",
        "html_line": 684,
        "anchor": "cabinet-tips",
        "section": "29.6.1"
      },
      {
        "level": 4,
        "text": "29.6.1.2 Multiple mics",
        "html_line": 684,
        "anchor": "multiple-mics",
        "section": "29.6.1.2"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 684,
    "anchor": "multiple-mics",
    "section": "29.6.1.2",
    "locator": "cabinet:B012"
  },
  {
    "device": "cabinet",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "A common studio technique is to use multiple mics on a single cabinet, and then adjust the balance during mixing. This is easy to do by using Live’s Audio Effect Racks. Try this:",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "29.6 Cabinet",
        "html_line": 662,
        "anchor": "cabinet",
        "section": "29.6"
      },
      {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "29.6.1 Cabinet Tips",
        "html_line": 684,
        "anchor": "cabinet-tips",
        "section": "29.6.1"
      },
      {
        "level": 4,
        "text": "29.6.1.2 Multiple mics",
        "html_line": 684,
        "anchor": "multiple-mics",
        "section": "29.6.1.2"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 684,
    "anchor": null,
    "section": null,
    "locator": "cabinet:B013"
  },
  {
    "device": "cabinet",
    "kind": "li",
    "text": "Configure one instance of Cabinet as you like.",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "29.6 Cabinet",
        "html_line": 662,
        "anchor": "cabinet",
        "section": "29.6"
      },
      {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "29.6.1 Cabinet Tips",
        "html_line": 684,
        "anchor": "cabinet-tips",
        "section": "29.6.1"
      },
      {
        "level": 4,
        "text": "29.6.1.2 Multiple mics",
        "html_line": 684,
        "anchor": "multiple-mics",
        "section": "29.6.1.2"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 684,
    "anchor": null,
    "section": null,
    "locator": "cabinet:B014"
  },
  {
    "device": "cabinet",
    "kind": "li",
    "text": "Put the Cabinet into an Audio Effect Rack.",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "29.6 Cabinet",
        "html_line": 662,
        "anchor": "cabinet",
        "section": "29.6"
      },
      {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "29.6.1 Cabinet Tips",
        "html_line": 684,
        "anchor": "cabinet-tips",
        "section": "29.6.1"
      },
      {
        "level": 4,
        "text": "29.6.1.2 Multiple mics",
        "html_line": 684,
        "anchor": "multiple-mics",
        "section": "29.6.1.2"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 684,
    "anchor": null,
    "section": null,
    "locator": "cabinet:B015"
  },
  {
    "device": "cabinet",
    "kind": "li",
    "text": "Duplicate the Rack chain that contains the original Cabinet as many times as you like.",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "29.6 Cabinet",
        "html_line": 662,
        "anchor": "cabinet",
        "section": "29.6"
      },
      {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "29.6.1 Cabinet Tips",
        "html_line": 684,
        "anchor": "cabinet-tips",
        "section": "29.6.1"
      },
      {
        "level": 4,
        "text": "29.6.1.2 Multiple mics",
        "html_line": 684,
        "anchor": "multiple-mics",
        "section": "29.6.1.2"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 684,
    "anchor": null,
    "section": null,
    "locator": "cabinet:B016"
  },
  {
    "device": "cabinet",
    "kind": "li",
    "text": "In the additional chains, choose a different Microphone setting and/or mic type.",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "29.6 Cabinet",
        "html_line": 662,
        "anchor": "cabinet",
        "section": "29.6"
      },
      {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "29.6.1 Cabinet Tips",
        "html_line": 684,
        "anchor": "cabinet-tips",
        "section": "29.6.1"
      },
      {
        "level": 4,
        "text": "29.6.1.2 Multiple mics",
        "html_line": 684,
        "anchor": "multiple-mics",
        "section": "29.6.1.2"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 684,
    "anchor": null,
    "section": null,
    "locator": "cabinet:B017"
  },
  {
    "device": "cabinet",
    "kind": "li",
    "text": "Adjust the relative volumes of the Rack’s chains in the Rack’s mixer.",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "29.6 Cabinet",
        "html_line": 662,
        "anchor": "cabinet",
